      {"id": "column_1", "type": "text", "x": 60, "y": 330, "width": 420, "height": 360, "z_index": 2, "content": "Solstice began in a small kitchen with a crate of bitter oranges. Every batch is still steeped slowly, then lightly carbonated so the botanicals stay bright. The result is a drink that tastes like late afternoon: warm, a little sharp, and gone too soon. We still press the citrus by hand on Mondays, and the whole street knows it by the smell.", "font_family": "Solstice Sans", "font_size": 22, "color": "rgba(34,30,28,1)", "line_height": 1.55, "style_runs": [{"start": 0, "end": 65, "font_weight": "bold"}]},
      {"id": "column_2", "type": "text", "x": 520, "y": 330, "width": 420, "height": 360, "z_index": 2, "content": "This season we added three flavors, each tied to an hour of the longest day. Citrus Dawn wakes you up, Berry Dusk winds you down, and Mint Noon sits in between. Serve them cold, over ice, and ideally outdoors. Each can is fully recyclable, and every label is printed with plant-based inks on paper from managed forests.", "font_family": "Solstice Sans", "font_size": 22, "color": "rgba(34,30,28,1)", "line_height": 1.55, "style_runs": [{"start": 77, "end": 88, "font_style": "italic"}, {"start": 103, "end": 113, "font_style": "italic"}, {"start": 134, "end": 143, "font_style": "italic"}]},
